# One Claude account on every machine (local-cswap, sd:7323). Remote Control
# sees only the sessions of the active account, so the machines must agree.
# Install it on every machine (common.cron). The hub, the machine whose
# `sd-db fence` reads holder, runs one `cswap auto --once --strategy
# consume-first` tick and publishes its account's organizationUuid in the
# workflow database; every other machine switches to its own account with
# that id. A promoted satellite reads holder, so it leads by itself.
#
# An unreadable hub, an unset row or an id no single account here has
# switches nothing and exits 1, graded data safe, so Today lists it and
# nothing pushes to the phone. A hub that refuses this machine's sd_db
# build skips the run until repo-sync follow catches up, and fails from
# the 30th such run in a row (system sd:7407). Each call is bounded
# (60 s, 120 s for the auto tick), well under JOB_TIMEOUT; a slot that
# finds the last run still active logs `skipped` and exits 0.
JOB_SCHEDULE="* * * * *"
JOB_TIMEOUT="5m"
JOB_COMMAND="bash \"$ROOT/../local-cswap/cswap.sh\" sync"
